1. Executive Summary
Customer churn is an important business problem for telecommunications providers because customers who leave reduce recurring revenue and may increase the cost of acquiring replacement customers. This project applies data analytics and machine learning to a publicly available Telco Customer Churn dataset. The work covers data preparation, exploratory analysis, visualization, feature engineering, classification, model evaluation, and business-oriented interpretation.
The analysis investigates customer tenure, charges, contracts, internet services, payment methods, support services, and other customer attributes. Three classification algorithms—Logistic Regression, Decision Tree, and Random Forest—are trained and compared using accuracy, precision, recall, F1-score, and ROC-AUC. The complete implementation is provided in the accompanying Jupyter Notebook.
